{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511826-demon-the-fallen-aura-of-misfortune","id":1511826,"title":"Demon the fallen - Aura of Misfortune","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-16T15:01:31-07:00","id":1511826,"title":"Demon the fallen - Aura of Misfortune","content":"The form ability &quot;Aura of Misfortune&quot; says, that any individual caught within a distance in yards equal to the demon's Torment score suffer a botch on any roll of 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> Im a bit confused...I always thought, that with this power, not only a 1 but also a 2 will cancel a rolled success...thats how it was translated in my German Core-Rulebook. But now, with the English Players-Guide in hand, I understand it to cause a botch, regardless of the number of successes, when there ist a 1 or 2 involved in the role.<br /> <br /> Which of the two options is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27257-wardoo","name":"Wardoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T03:05:26-07:00","id":1511850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wardoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511826-demon-the-fallen-aura-of-misfortune#post1511826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The form ability &quot;Aura of Misfortune&quot; says, that any individual caught within a distance in yards equal to the demon's Torment score suffer a botch on any roll of 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> Im a bit confused...I always thought, that with this power, not only a 1 but also a 2 will cancel a rolled success...thats how it was translated in my German Core-Rulebook. But now, with the English Players-Guide in hand, I understand it to cause a botch, regardless of the number of successes, when there ist a 1 or 2 involved in the role.<br /> <br /> Which of the two options is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Causing a botch regardless of the number of successes is definitely <b>Not</b> the intended function. Aura of misfortune just extends the normal botch rules so that rolling any 2's must be counted with rolled 1's when measuring for a botch.<br /> <br /> The english text is just using a shorthand to try to convey that in as few words as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}